 The system should allow regional authors to publish locale-specific content without affecting other storefronts. | Confirmed |  |\n| HPC-008 | Homepage & Content | Content Model & CMS Authoring | The system should support a full-width hero banner with CMS-managed imagery, copy and CTA links. | Confirmed |  |\n| HPC-009 | Homepage & Content | Content Model & CMS Authoring | The system should support editorial modules including campaign imagery, collection features and product spotlights. | Confirmed |  |\n| HPC-010 | Homepage & Content | Content Model & CMS Authoring | The system should support reusable page builder templates across page types. | Confirmed |  |\n| HPC-011 | Homepage & Content | Content Model & CMS Authoring | The system should support a global and local content model where some content is global (e.g. Sustainability, Fashion Show Hub pages) and some is localised (e.g. policy pages). | Confirmed |  |\n| HPC-012 | Homepage & Content | Content Model & CMS Authoring | The system should support live stream embedding on editorial pages via a structured CMS solution, replacing the current approach of raw HTML code snippets. | Confirmed |  |\n| HPC-013 | Homepage & Content | Consent & Cookie Management | The system should grey out all site content and prevent interaction with all site elements when the Didomi consent notice is displayed. | Confirmed |  |\n| HPC-014 | Homepage & Content | Consent & Cookie Management | The system should remove the grey out effect and restore full site interactivity once the customer has completed the Didomi consent flow. | Confirmed |  |\n| HPC-015 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system should display a sticky global header visible at the top of the screen on all pages and devices. | Confirmed | Open Discussion: Header sticky / non-sticky - pending motion design as well @Jasmijn Tsang |\n| HPC-016 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system should display the Zimmermann brand logo linking back to the homepage. | Confirmed |  |\n| HPC-017 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system should display a rotating promotional announcement banner above the header managed via the CMS. | Confirmed |  |\n| HPC-018 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system should display the following clickable icons in the header: Locate Boutique, Contact Us, Newsletter, Search, Account and Bag. | Confirmed |  |\n| HPC-019 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system should display a Wishlist icon that navigates anonymous customers to the login page. | Confirmed |  |\n| HPC-020 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system should display a Wishlist icon that navigates logged in customers to the wishlist page. | Confirmed |  |\n| HPC-021 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system should display a Bag icon with a running count of items in the customer's bag. | Confirmed |  |\n| HPC-022 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system should display top-level navigation categories linking to the relevant product listing pages. | Confirmed |  |\n| HPC-023 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The systems should display a 'Back in Boutique' navigation category to show customer items that will be in the boutique | Confirmed | Additional Notes: this is a manually created category by content team  @Jasmijn Tsang |\n| HPC-024 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system will display a mega menu on desktop when a customer hovers over a navigation category, with the exception of Z.Immerse which will function as a direct link to a page | Confirmed |  |\n| HPC-025 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system should display a hamburger menu on mobile to access navigation categories. | Confirmed |  |\n| HPC-026 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system should display a country/region selector in the header to allow customers to switch locale and country excluding the AU store. | Confirmed |  |\n| HPC-027 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system should persist the customer's selected region across sessions. | Confirmed |  |\n| HPC-028 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system should allow the business user to add and remove navigation items without requiring a code change. | Confirmed |  |\n| HPC-029 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system should support cloning of the global navigation structure across markets. | Confirmed |  |\n| HPC-030 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Footer | The system should display a global footer with content managed via the CMS. | Confirmed | Footer edibility per storefront |\n| HPC-031 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Footer | The system should display footer navigation links. | Confirmed |  |\n| HPC-032 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Footer | The system should navigate the customer to the relevant page or destination when a footer link is clicked. | Confirmed |  |\n| HPC-033 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Footer | The system should display copyright and legal text in the footer. | Confirmed |  |\n| HPC-034 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Footer | The system should display a \"Join Us\" email capture field in the footer. | Confirmed |  |\n| HPC-035 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Footer | The system should display a modal on clicking the Continue CTA to collect the customer's first name and last name. | Confirmed |  |\n| HPC-036 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Footer | The system should pass email sign-up data to Omneo (who will then pass to Emarsys) | Confirmed |  |\n| HPC-037 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Footer | The system should display appropriate privacy consent copy and a link to the local Privacy Policy on the sign-up modal. | Confirmed | Additional Note: Should display Accessibility  @Jasmijn Tsang |\n| HPC-038 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Footer | The system should allow business users to add region specific footer links (e.g Acknowledgement of Country for AU storefront). | Confirmed |  |\n|  | Homepage & Content | Chat Integration | The system should display the chat widget as a pop-up overlay on the relevant pages. Page visibility rules are determined by Inside Chat. | Confirmed |  |\n| HPC-040 | Homepage & Content | Chat Integration | The system should only initialise the chat widget after the customer has consented to the relevant cookie category via Didomi. | Confirmed |  |",
